 and clicking Save was accepted; dashboard now shows Wedding Date 'Jan 1, 2020' instead of rejecting the invalid past date and keeping the previous Sep 20, 2027\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"View Details/View Profile buttons do not open listing details\", \"actual\": \"Clicking 'View Details' on a venue card (e.g. Rosewood Garden Estate) and 'View Profile' on a vendor card (e.g. Eternal Moments Photography) produced no visible change - no modal, no navigation, no expanded detail view. URL, DOM, and network requests remained unchanged after the click.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Checking the \\\"Set a budget\\\" task checkbox in \\\"12+ Months Before\\\" immediately updated its Progress from 0% to 17% (1/6). After saving the checklist to Dashboard, the Dashboard's aggregate \\\"Planning Progress\\\" stat also showed 17% and the saved-checklist preview showed \\\"1 of 6 completed\\\". After a full page reload, the checked state, 17% checklist progress, and 17% aggregate dashboard progress all remained unchanged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking filter chips immediately updated visible results and the 'Showing X of Y' count without any submit button; clearing all filters restored the full list immediately.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Cancelled draft persists in editor on reopen\", \"actual\": \"After editing Partner One to 'Sam' and clicking Cancel, dashboard correctly kept 'Alex & Jordan'. But reopening the editor via Update Details showed Partner One field pre-filled with 'Sam' (the cancelled draft) instead of 'Alex' (the last saved value).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard shows couple names 'Alex & Taylor',